3 to form a chow, which is possible. So they still have potential. So F4 seems the weakest.\n\nAlso, looking at prevailing wind West (F3) and seat wind East (F1), my F4 is not a prevailing or seat wind, so no extra points. So discarding F4 is safe.\n\nI'll choose Play F4.\n\nReason: Discarding F4 removes an isolated honor tile that currently does not contribute to forming melds or pairs, and it does not match the prevailing or seat winds. Keeping the connected suited tiles (W1-W2, T4-T5-T6, B4) offers more flexibility for forming chows and potentially completing a hand with patterns like All Types if a dragon tile is drawn later.\n\nAnswer: Play F4"}
